NEKO TERMINAL

This is a read-only Linux-inspired shell for exploring the site.

GETTING STARTED
  ls /                  List the virtual root
  tree /blogs           Browse every post
  cd /blogs             Change the working directory
  cat path/to/post.md   Read Markdown source
  glow path/to/post.md  Render Markdown and images in the terminal

SHELL FEATURES
  Paths, quoted arguments, wildcards, and pipelines are supported.
  Use Up/Down for history, Tab for completion, and Ctrl+L to clear.
  Ctrl+C cancels the current line or a running command.

COMMANDS
  basename  cat    cd      clear   cut      dirname  echo   exit
  find      glow   grep    head    help     ls       nl     printf
  pwd       sed    sort    tail    tr       tree     uniq   wc     which

EXAMPLES
  find /blogs -type f -name '*.md'
  grep -in terminal /blogs/**/*.md | head -n 5
  cat /blogs/notes/hello-terminal.md
  glow /blogs/notes/hello-terminal.md
  printf '%s\n' alpha beta beta | sort | uniq -c

The filesystem is generated from this repository. Add Markdown and image
files under blogs/ to publish them on the next deployment.

